		{"id":"b15fb411d952e5d4","type":"text","text":"How do we define intelligence?","x":-140,"y":20,"width":280,"height":50,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"7d6d450f7274ed04","type":"text","text":"> “Every aspect of learning or any other feature of intelligence can in principle be so precisely described that a machine can be made to simulate it.”\n\n  \n— John McCarthy et al., \"A Proposal for the Dartmouth Summer Research Project on Artificial Intelligence,\" 1955","x":-176,"y":500,"width":347,"height":123},
		{"id":"7c89e4022dc01c20","type":"text","text":"Why do we define intelligence?","x":-140,"y":380,"width":276,"height":60,"color":"2"},
